# Built by packaging/build-guacd.sh from the Apache release tarball. Not
# committed: it is a ~350 KB binary that anyone can reproduce with one
# command, the script pins and checks the source digest, and a binary in git
# is a thing reviewers cannot read. The ISO build and a 26.04 native install
# both call the script.
packaging/guacd-debs/

# The upstream Guacamole tree, unpacked here by build-guacd.sh so the build
# can COPY it in (extracting inside an emulated amd64 container fails on
# every file). The script removes it when it finishes, but a commit made
# WHILE a build is running would otherwise sweep ~30 MB of third-party
# source into the repo — which nearly happened, hence this line.
packaging/dockerfiles/guacd/src/
